<!-- CONTACT FORM -->
List of Processes:
Form Submission Interception

The form submission is caught by the submit event listener, preventing the form from being submitted in the usual way.
Prevent Default Form Submission

event.preventDefault() stops the form from submitting and refreshing the page immediately.
Clear Previous Error Messages

Any previous error messages are cleared out so old errors don't show up again.
Retrieve Input Values

The code grabs the values from the input fields (name, email, message).
Initialize Validation Check

A variable (valid) is set to true, assuming everything is correct initially.
Name Field Validation

The code checks if the name field is empty and shows an error message if it is.
Email Field Validation

The code checks if the email field is empty and shows an error message if it is.
Email Format Validation

The code uses a regular expression (regex) to ensure the email is in a valid format (like "someone@example.com"). If it’s not, it shows an error message.
Message Field Validation

The code checks if the message field is empty and shows an error message if it is.
Validation Passes

If all fields are filled out and valid (name, email, and message are correct), the form is considered ready to be sent.
Prepare Data for Sending

The form data (name, email, message) is packaged into an object (params) to send to the email service (emailjs).
Send Form Data using emailjs

The emailjs service is used to send the form data using the service ID and template ID.
Handle Successful Email Send

If the email is sent successfully:
The form fields (name, email, and message) are cleared.
A success message is shown using a SweetAlert2 popup.
Handle Email Sending Error

If there’s an error while trying to send the email:
An error message is shown using a SweetAlert2 popup.
The error is logged in the console for debugging.
Summary of Key Processes:
Interception & Prevention: Stop the form from submitting automatically.
Validation: Check if name, email, and message fields are properly filled.
Email Sending: Use emailjs to send the form data if validation passes.
Feedback: Display success or error messages based on the email sending outcome.
These processes ensure that the form works correctly and provides feedback to the user in case of any issues.












